<%#
  The sidebar tree (PRD §7.6) — the primary navigation, present on every view.

  Two axes, deliberately (§6). The board answers *what have I touched lately*;
  this answers *where did I put that*. Which is why it lists notes
  individually rather than only folders: a folder row on its own makes finding
  one known note a two-step guess.

  Three things share one row shape — views, folders and notes — at one height,
  with depth carried by indentation alone. Rows that vary in height cannot be
  scanned vertically, which is the whole value of the tree over the board.

  The `filing` controller is mounted on the shell, not here: a card is dragged
  from the main pane onto a row in this one, so one controller has to see both.

  Deliberately not `role="tree"`. Real tree semantics promise arrow-key
  navigation, typeahead and roving tabindex, and a half-implemented tree is
  worse to a screen reader than an honest list of links and buttons — which is
  what this is, and which is already keyboard-reachable in source order. If
  the tree ever grows to the depth where that promise is worth keeping, it is
  worth keeping properly.
%>
<aside class="rail" aria-label="Notes and folders" data-controller="tree">
  <nav class="rail__group" aria-label="Views">
    <%= link_to root_path, class: "row row--view",
          "aria-current": (@folder.nil? && @note.nil? && controller_name == "notes" ? "page" : nil),
          data: { folder_id: "",
                  action: "dragenter->filing#over dragover->filing#over " \
                          "dragleave->filing#leave drop->filing#drop" } do %>
      <span class="row__twist row__twist--icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "icons/material_symbol", name: :notes %></span>
      <span class="row__label">Notes</span>
    <% end %>

    <%# Each of these becomes a link at the milestone that builds it. %>
    <span class="row row--view row--pending" title="Milestone 6">
      <span class="row__twist row__twist--icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "icons/material_symbol", name: :calendar %></span>
      <span class="row__label">Calendar</span>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <div class="rail__group">
    <h2 class="rail__heading">Folders</h2>

    <% @tree.branches.each do |branch| %>
      <%= render "folders/row", folder: branch.folder, notes: branch.notes %>

      <div class="rail__children"
           id="<%= dom_id(branch.folder, :notes) %>"
           data-tree-target="children"
           data-folder-id="<%= branch.folder.id %>">
        <% branch.notes.each do |note| %>
          <%= render "layouts/rail_note", note: note %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# Unfiled notes sit at the root of the tree, below the folders, so
        nothing in the account is unreachable from the sidebar (§7.6). %>
    <div class="rail__root-notes" data-folder-id="">
      <% @tree.unfiled.each do |note| %>
        <%= render "layouts/rail_note", note: note, root: true %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%= form_with model: Folder.new, class: "rail__new" do |form| %>
      <span class="row__twist row__twist--icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "icons/material_symbol", name: :add %></span>
      <%= form.text_field :name, placeholder: "New folder", class: "rail__new-field",
            autocomplete: "off", "aria-label": "New folder name" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="rail__group">
    <span class="row row--view row--pending" title="Milestone 8">
      <span class="row__twist row__twist--icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "icons/material_symbol", name: :archive %></span>
      <span class="row__label">Archive</span>
    </span>
    <span class="row row--view row--pending" title="Milestone 8">
      <span class="row__twist row__twist--icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "icons/material_symbol", name: :delete %></span>
      <span class="row__label">Trash</span>
    </span>
  </div>

</aside>
